SUMMARY:Elevating Your Research Through Software Development - R-Ladies+ Melbourne
DESCRIPTION:**Elevating Your Research Through Software Development**\n\n**Date:** 22nd September, 2026\n**Time:** 5:30 PM (networking and refreshments from 5:30 PM; talk begins at 6:00 PM)\n**Where:** DiUS, Level 3/31 Queen St, Melbourne\n\nResearch projects often begin with a collection of scripts and files that become increasingly difficult to manage, reproduce, and share. Adopting software development practices and structuring research projects like software packages can help address these challenges while improving the quality, reproducibility, and impact of research.\n\nIn this meetup, we’ll explore how package-based project structures can transform analytical workflows, using real-world examples from COVID-19 vaccination policy analysis and scabies transmission modelling in the Netherlands. The talk will demonstrate how treating research code as software enables more efficient collaboration, easier reuse, and faster translation of analyses into real-world decision-making. We’ll also discuss how emerging AI tools, such as Claude Code, can help researchers build resources that extend the reach of their work beyond its original scope.\n\nCome along if you’re interested in reproducible research, scientific programming, data analysis, or research software engineering, or if you’d like practical guidance on creating more structured, reusable, and collaborative research projects!
LOCATION:DiUS, Level 3, 31 Queen St, Melbourne, AUSTRALIA
URL:https://www.meetup.com/rladies-melbourne/events/316322495/
ORGANIZER;CN=R-Ladies+ Melbourne:mailto:info@rladies.org
CATEGORIES:RLadies+,R-Ladies+ Melbourne
